; =====================================================================
; module-directives.abnf
;
; VERBATIM.  These are draft-ietf-cbor-cddl-modules-07's own bytes, copied
; unchanged, including the Internet-Draft's three-column left margin.  It
; was NOT authored by this project.  Do not edit it, do not correct it, do
; not reformat it.  Defects found in it are recorded in README.md and in
; grammar-gaps.derived.txt, never repaired here.  The companion file that
; mechanically removes the margin so an ABNF tool can read it is
; module-directives-dedented.derived.abnf.
;
; Locator:  draft-ietf-cbor-cddl-modules-07, "CDDL Module Structure",
;           Bormann & Moran, 2 September 2026, Intended status: Standards
;           Track, Expires 6 March 2027.  Appendix A, "ABNF
;           Specification".  Source text lines 677-688 (one unbroken
;           region: no page frame falls inside it).
;           <https://www.ietf.org/archive/id/draft-ietf-cbor-cddl-modules-07.txt>
;
; Source digest (sha256 of the full cached source text):
;   7cf825aaad43d3d4995bcd540d3865ee3f69dd3dd453be5761a02c009458a644
; Region digest (sha256 of lines 677-688 exactly as below, no trailing
; newline added):
;   43c17148af31265a171f2e722b24d2e0063d0ab253d8b681cc1c223d5df696ab
;
; Appendix A's own introduction, verbatim: "This section specifies the
; grammar employed by the module structure directives using the ABNF
; language defined in [STD68] and [RFC7405]."
;
; TEN productions.  This grammar covers the DIRECTIVE line only.  It is
; not a grammar of CDDL and does not replace or amend RFC 8610 Appendix
; B; the CDDL a module file contains is basic CDDL and is parsed by RFC
; 8610's grammar.
;
; READ grammar-gaps.derived.txt BEFORE RELYING ON THIS FILE.  Three
; things in it do not hold as written: `id` admits neither "-" nor "."
; and therefore cannot match `cose.label` or `cose.empty_or_serialized_map`
; as used in this document's own Section 2.6 examples; `CRLF` is
; redefined here as `%x0A / %x0D.0A`, which admits a bare LF where STD
; 68's core rule is CR LF; and `directive` requires a space after ";#"
; where Section 2.3's prose requires only the prefix.
; =====================================================================

   directive = ";#" RS (%s"import" / %s"include") RS [from-clause]
                       filename [as-clause] CRLF
   from-clause = 1*(id-or-all [","] RS) %s"from" RS
   as-clause = RS %s"as" RS id
   filename = 1*("-" / "." / %x30-39 / %x41-5a / "_" / %x61-7a)
   id = ("$" / %x40-5a / "_" / %x61-7a)
        *("$" / %x30-39 / %x40-5a / "_" / %x61-7a)
   id-or-all = id / "*"
   RS = 1*WS
   WS = SP
   SP = %x20
   CRLF = %x0A / %x0D.0A
